      "problem": "What are the radius $r$ and the coordinates of the center $C$ for the sphere ${x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2}+(z-1)^{2}=2?$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the equation of a sphere centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ with radius $r>0$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-{x}_{0})^{2}+(y-{y}_{0})^{2}+(z-{z}_{0})^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can write our equation as\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2}+(z-1)^{2}=(\\sqrt{2})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives us the center at the point point $C(0,-3,1)$ and the radius $r=\\sqrt{2}.$",
